-- title:
--   Components of the geometric fibre are determined by their chart prime
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an integer $M \neq 0$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ for the set $\{p\}$, and let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the image of the function field `x1FunctionFieldC ℚ (Gamma1 (M * p))` under the coefficientwise map $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q} \to \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with $L$ as fraction field, such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A \to L$; let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with the tower $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ the $q$-expansion $\mathrm{coeffEmb}_L(\mathrm{jq})$, where $\mathrm{jq} = q^{-1} \cdot \mathrm{jNumQ}$. Finally let $k$ be an algebraically closed field which is an $A$-algebra. Write $X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ for [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252), the map out of the pushout of the two affine charts $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $A$-subalgebras of $K$ generated by $j$ and by $j^{-1}$, and let $X_k = X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} A} \operatorname{Spec} k$ with first projection $\mathrm{pr}_1$. The assertion is: for all subsets $Z_1, Z_2$ of the underlying space of $X_k$ that are irreducible components, and every point $y$ of the finite chart $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $A$-subalgebra generated by $j$, if the image of $y$ under the base map of [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.ιFin A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L231) equals $\mathrm{pr}_1$ of the generic point of $Z_1$ and also $\mathrm{pr}_1$ of the generic point of $Z_2$, then $Z_1 = Z_2$.
--
--   This is the statement that an irreducible component of a geometric fibre of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\operatorname{Spec} A$ is determined by the prime of the finite chart lying under its generic point; for the special fibre it encodes that the two Igusa components are already defined over the residue field, while over the generic point the geometric fibre is irreducible and the assertion is vacuous. It serves as the injectivity input to the downstream analysis of the components of the special fibre, in particular to the statements on crossings, on the action of the diamond automorphisms and on the image of the finite chart.
